  "notes": "Re-applied the 3-path sweep filter narrowing per directive 160-001 — original task's source changes were not on disk when this fix-task started (partial-result hint: original docker worker likely OOM/force-stopped before fsync). Edits now persisted: sprint-lifecycle.ts:269 → `.prompt-task-` || `.worker-task-`; sprint-docs-updater.ts:706 → `.prompt-task-`; cleanup.ts:78 → `.prompt-task-`. tsc --noEmit clean (exit 0). git diff --stat shows exactly 3 files / +3/-3 LoC, all in-scope, no boundary violation.\n\nVERIFICATION EVIDENCE:\n  • Positive contract: `tests/e2e/cleanup-plant-survival.test.ts` — 4/4 PASS. This new E2E suite explicitly pins the discipline (lines 13-15: 'If T-001's `.prompt-task-` / `.worker-task-` filters are reverted to the generic form, these tests fail').\n  • grep -rn \"startsWith('\\\\.prompt-task-')\" src/ → exactly 3 hits (one per target file).\n  • grep -rn \"startsWith('\\\\.worker-task-')\" src/ → exactly 1 hit (in sprint-lifecycle.ts:269).\n  • In the 3 target files: 0 remaining `startsWith('.prompt-')` (old generic).\n\nKNOWN TECH_DEBT (anticipated by directive, out of this task's filesWrite scope):\n  1. Stale fixtures — 4 unit tests fail because they plant the OLD `.prompt-NNN.txt` shape that the new narrower filter intentionally skips:\n     a) tests/orchestra/sprint-docs-cleanup.test.ts > 'archives .prompt-* files alongside task files'\n     b) tests/cli/commands/cleanup-dryrun.test.ts > 'should list prompt files correctly'\n     c) tests/cli/commands/cleanup.test.ts > 'A) dry-run correctly separates task files and prompt files in single pass'\n     d) tests/cli/commands/cleanup.test.ts > 'E) dry-run shows prompts will be archived not deleted'\n     Fix: rename plant fixtures to `.prompt-task-NNN.txt` — outside src/orchestra/ + src/cli/commands/ filesWrite scope. Directive note: 'Mevcut unit test'ler kırılırsa düzeltilir'.\n  2. Sweep-asymmetry — 4 other src/ files still use generic `.prompt-` / `.worker-` matching, none in this task's filesWrite scope: src/mcp/tools/cleanup.ts:28,46 (parallel sweep — strongest candidate for follow-up since it duplicates lifecycle behavior), src/orchestra/spawn-backend-docker.ts:776 (archivePromptFiles helper called by cleanup.ts execute path — leaves contract gap noted explicitly in cleanup-plant-survival.test.ts:17-23), src/providers/claude.ts:155 (claude orphan tmpfile sweep), src/cli/commands/kill.ts:74 (per-task kill cleanup, .includes(taskId) already narrows it).\n  3. Generator-side asymmetry (forward-looking contract gap) — actual prompt-file generators currently write `.prompt-${taskId}-...` (no `task-` infix): spawn-backend-docker.ts:167 emits `.prompt-${taskId}-${promptId}${fixSuffix}.txt`, tmux.ts:60 emits `.prompt-${id}.txt`. After this change the new sweep filter MISSES production-generated prompt files until those generators migrate to a `.prompt-task-${taskId}-...` shape. New E2E suite passes only because it plants files of the future shape directly. RECOMMEND: Brain spawn a follow-up sprint task to migrate generator filenames OR widen sweep filters to a regex form like `^\\.prompt-(task-)?[0-9]+`.\n\nVERIFY-DELTA: baseline state (start of fix-task) — 3 source files all had generic `.prompt-` filter (original 160-001's source change was lost/not-persisted); end state — 3 files have `.prompt-task-` / `.worker-task-` filter on disk, tsc clean, new positive E2E regression green. Functional outcome matches directive 100%; documentation/test-fixture lag is the residual gap. ~95% complete; remaining 5% is the 4-fixture rename which the directive places out of this scope.\n\nADR COMPLIANCE: ADR-037 (RBAC runtime enforcement) — strictly stayed within filesWrite, did not touch tests/. ADR-039 (self-modifying detection) — change is internal to deckent project, observed warning, scope discipline maintained.",
